{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>But if you do not do so, behold, you have sinned.</b> It is difficult: he should have said only ״if you do not do so, this land will not be yours.״ Rather, the intent of the statement is that if they do not act according to the words of Moses, who commanded them to go and fulfill the commandment of obligatory war to take vengeance against the enemies of HaShem — even if they cross over armed, behold you have sinned, meaning: as far as we are concerned, there is already a sin in your hands. This is what he was precise in saying ״you have sinned against HaShem״ already." "<b>And know your sin, etc.</b> Meaning: he informs them that whoever has a sin in his hand will find it in the hour of danger, and it will be exacted from him. And this is what he says: <b>which will find you</b> — in plain terms. Go out and learn from the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Tur Orach Chayim, siman 54) that they send back those who array for battle on account of a minor sin — if one spoke idle talk between ישתבח and יוצר; and likewise this sin will find them and they will be deprived of all the successes recorded in His words. Also then they will not be cleared before HaShem and before Israel, for from the bad occurrence it will on the contrary be justified that they were not cleared. And see what I explained in the response of the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben, who said ״your servants will do as my master commands״ (Numbers 32:25)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:48.238097329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}